Z||000000||88TransAmGTA||08-09-2001||12:26 AM|||| Hi all, First off I don't have a fiero but I saw something amazing last weekend I thought you should know about.<P> I was at the local track and a Fiero with a stock supercharged 3.8 out of a grand prix or something was up against a Ferrari 355, I thought to myself haha that Fiero is dead. When the lights turned green the fiero got a litle lead on the 355 but lost it at the 1/8 mark BUT the litlt Fiero stayed right with the 355 and only lost by .3 it was amazing, I want a fiero now!!<P> Just think about it a fiero that costs maybe $2,000 and the engine conveersion that prob runs around $10,000?? that keeps up with a $120,000 car WoW!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||pHoOl||08-09-2001||12:35 AM||||Welcome to the board!!!  Yeah, Fieros are very flexible on engine conversions.  Many people have put vette engines in, and cadillac northstars.  Plus, tack on about another 10 grand to your figure, and you would have a car that looks exactly like a ferrari 355 too!<P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroKyle||08-09-2001||12:41 AM||||The 350 V-8 engines are popular. Stock you can get 300 to 350 hp which is not to far off what the 355 is running. For that conversion plus a good Fiero your looking at $15,000. Thats a brand new V-8 and installed for you by Archie.||||reg||1
