Z||000006||rogergarrison||08-09-2001||01:32 PM||||ya got same approx HP with 1,000 less pnds to haul around. All european cars are geared for high speed, not short sprints. American cars seldom have to pass 70 mph speed limit, so there geared for that. I had an older Z-28 (maybe 76?) had like 4:? gears wouldnt go over 120.......but got there really quick. Now take your average muscle car and try to keep up with the Ferrari on a roadcourse like Mid-Ohio....... Comparing to Fiero on handling though would be quite close. If I remember right, a stock 308 GTB only runs mid 14s in a 1/4 mile.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jay||08-09-2001||01:58 PM||||Roger you are so right.  All Italian cars are geared for top end that's why they are true GT's (Grand Turismo...Grand tourers).  On the highway, the real deal wins everytime, I don't care what kind of conversion you got.  For instance, at the 1/4 mile track I beat a Lotus esprit, but give it more than 1/4 mile and I think the lotus would kick my butt.  If you've never driven an Italian sportscar, you don't know what you are missing.  My advice, rent a Ferrari for the week-end once in your life, you'll be sold.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dave Gunsul||08-09-2001||08:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison: an older Z-28 (maybe 76?) had like 4:? gears <P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-09-2001).][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hate to be a nit-picker but there was no Z28 in 75-76. The Z was dropped after 74 and then brought back as a 77 1/2 model.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||08-10-2001||04:58 AM||||Jay, you're right, all I have to say is <P>"This is why you have to drive a ferrari before you die"  <P>Those of you whom have had the pleasure<BR>know what I am talking about.<P>(PS: I that guy with the 355 could drive, with my 5-speed northstar I figure I am going to be a litte behind, but almost able to keep up... at best.  <P>I've had the extreme pleasure of driving a 355 Spyder, they are simple THE FINEST automobile on the planet.  Nothing else even remotely like it. Yes, yes, yes, OH MY GOD YES!!!!!  Peroid. ;)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
